# Keep host-installed dependencies and build output out of the Docker build context.
#
# The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and then `COPY . .`. Without this file the
# host's frontend/node_modules (installed by a different npm/Node, OS or
# lockfile state) is copied over the clean `npm ci` install, so the image
# can end up with a vite and rolldown pair that don't match each other and
# fail while loading vite.config.ts.
node_modules
dist
.vite
*.tsbuildinfo
